From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:16:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: zero os_alloc_mem() allocations

os_alloc_mem() backs the RM heap (portMemAllocNonPaged() and friends)
with kmalloc() or vmalloc() and returns the memory uninitialized. There
are about 560 portMemAllocNonPaged() call sites in RM; whether all of
them initialize everything they later read cannot reasonably be
checked. Most distribution kernels enable init_on_alloc, so the memory
is zeroed in practice, and a kernel without it may expose code paths
that depend on that.

Zero the allocations in os_alloc_mem() with __GFP_ZERO. With
init_on_alloc set this costs nothing extra, the allocator only zeroes
once. Without it, RM behaves as it does on a kernel with
init_on_alloc, while the rest of the system keeps the cheaper
uninitialized allocations.

GPU system memory (nv_alloc_pages()) is not affected; it is zeroed
by the driver as long as NVreg_InitializeSystemMemoryAllocations
keeps its default of 1. nvidia-modeset and nvidia-uvm have their own
allocators and are not covered by this change.

[Also zero the order 1 to 5 kmalloc() attempt that
"nvidia: don't retry high-order kmalloc in os_alloc_mem()" added,
with a new NV_KZALLOC_NORETRY().]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 819622c556cda388c8c447a7c96d0536f817b896)
---
 kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c | 13 +++++++++----
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h b/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h
index 636215a5..c90679b4 100644
--- a/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h
+++ b/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h
@@ -451,6 +451,24 @@ static NvBool nv_numa_node_has_memory(int node_id)
         NV_MEMDBG_ADD(ptr, size);              \
     }
 
+#define NV_KZALLOC_ATOMIC(ptr, size) \
+    { \
+        (ptr) = kzalloc(size, NV_GFP_ATOMIC); \
+        NV_MEMDBG_ADD(ptr, size);             \
+    }
+
+#define NV_KZALLOC_NO_OOM(ptr, size) \
+    { \
+        (ptr) = kzalloc(size, NV_GFP_NO_OOM); \
+        NV_MEMDBG_ADD(ptr, size);             \
+    }
+
+#define NV_KZALLOC_NORETRY(ptr, size) \
+    { \
+        (ptr) = kzalloc(size, NV_GFP_NORETRY); \
+        NV_MEMDBG_ADD(ptr, size);              \
+    }
+
 #define NV_KFREE(ptr, size) \
     { \
         NV_MEMDBG_REMOVE(ptr, size); \
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c
index 73a609f1..673f3632 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c
@@ -642,16 +642,21 @@ NV_STATUS NV_API_CALL os_alloc_mem(
     if (alloc_size != size)
         return NV_ERR_INVALID_PARAMETER;
 
+    //
+    // Return zeroed memory, so that RM behaves the same whether or not the
+    // kernel runs with init_on_alloc. The allocator does not zero twice when
+    // init_on_alloc is set.
+    //
     if (!NV_MAY_SLEEP())
     {
         if (alloc_size <= KMALLOC_LIMIT)
-            NV_KMALLOC_ATOMIC(*address, alloc_size);
+            NV_KZALLOC_ATOMIC(*address, alloc_size);
     }
     else
     {
         if (alloc_size <= PAGE_SIZE)
         {
-            NV_KMALLOC_NO_OOM(*address, alloc_size);
+            NV_KZALLOC_NO_OOM(*address, alloc_size);
         }
         else if (alloc_size <= KMALLOC_LIMIT)
         {
@@ -660,11 +665,11 @@ NV_STATUS NV_API_CALL os_alloc_mem(
             // retry reclaim and compaction for it, we fall back to vmalloc
             // anyway. This follows kvmalloc().
             //
-            NV_KMALLOC_NORETRY(*address, alloc_size);
+            NV_KZALLOC_NORETRY(*address, alloc_size);
         }
         if (*address == NULL)
         {
-            *address = nv_vmalloc(alloc_size, GFP_KERNEL);
+            *address = nv_vmalloc(alloc_size, GFP_KERNEL | __GFP_ZERO);
             alloc_size |= VMALLOC_ALLOCATION_SIZE_FLAG;
         }
     }
